diff --git a/docs/ai-passport-ble-protocol.md b/docs/ai-passport-ble-protocol.md
index 73dab77..278c927 100644
--- a/docs/ai-passport-ble-protocol.md
+++ b/docs/ai-passport-ble-protocol.md
@@ -89,15 +89,26 @@ sending `"host":"passvoice"` in `host_ready`. Both `DOWN` and `OK` report
 `click` or `long` through `button_event`. Each key uses its own 650 ms hold
 timer, including after a quick tap. The hold is the only event for that press.
 Only an `UP` click can end capture in this mode. `DOWN` and `OK` gestures
-that begin or trigger during
-capture are suppressed. A fresh press can trigger immediately after `UP`
-requests the stop. If the worker has not finished sending `ptt_up`, that
-`button_event` includes an optional `sessionId` for the stopped capture. The
-notification may arrive before `ptt_down` or `ptt_up`. The host uses the
-session ID to wait for a matching normal stop before acting on a deferred
-Return. Firmware predating this mode ignores the optional `host` field.
-Firmware predating `DOWN` hold support reports only its `click` event. Other
-hosts retain the mapping above, with `DOWN` reporting only clicks.
+that begin or trigger during capture are suppressed. A fresh press can trigger
+immediately after `UP` requests the stop. The audio worker queues its
+`button_event` after successfully queueing `ptt_up`, with an optional
+`sessionId` identifying the capture if the gesture triggered before
+`ptt_up` was sent. The worker discards these gestures on capture failure
+or a change of session or connection. Earlier firmware could notify
+a tagged gesture before `ptt_down` or `ptt_up`. The host uses the tag
+to associate a deferred Return with the matching normal stop.
+
+PassVoice owns the editing bindings and the timing of text actions. The display
+may show the existing VOICE, SEND and UNDO hints on a physical press. They
+identify the keys and do not reflect customized bindings or confirm an edit.
+The firmware uses Recording and Processing for capture and its normal stop.
+The host resumes Ready after it finishes audio playback. Text can still be
+committing on the Mac at that point, and the firmware does not show an edit
+result for DOWN or OK in PassVoice mode.
+
+Firmware predating PassVoice mode ignores the optional `host` field. Firmware
+predating DOWN hold support reports only its `click` event. Other hosts retain
+the mapping above, with DOWN reporting only clicks.

